cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GearScript in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "GearScript: a CSS-like language for describing and animating mechanisms"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Murali
    given-names: Sivaprasad
version: 1.0.0-beta
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://gearscript.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hypertoroid/GearScript"
abstract: >-
  GearScript is a small, CSS-like language and browser-based studio for describing
  mechanisms and animating them in 3D. Parts are connected by hinges, sliders, pins,
  gears and belts, and a solver closes every loop at every frame, so connected parts
  move the way real ones would. Projects are plain text, and the toolchain reports
  numbered errors with fixes, which lets people and AI models write and correct them.
keywords:
  - animation
  - mechanisms
  - kinematics
  - domain-specific language
  - education
  - visualization
